# Mizan

A daily balance and growth app: four pillars, seven identities, a 40-day journey, per-prayer tracking and a 60-second evening check-in.

Single-page web app, no build step, no server. Your data stays in your browser (localStorage).

## Files

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `index.html` | The whole app |
| `manifest.webmanifest` | Makes it installable (name, icons, colours) |
| `service-worker.js` | Offline support; loads the newest version when online |
| `icon-192.png`, `icon-512.png` | App icons |

## Deploy on GitHub Pages

1. Put all files in the repository root.
2. Settings → Pages → Deploy from a branch → `main` / `(root)`.
3. Open `https://<username>.github.io/<repo>/`.

> Pages on a private repository needs a paid GitHub plan. On a free plan, make the repo public (nothing personal is stored in it; user data never leaves the device).

## Install on iPhone

Open the site in Safari → Share → Add to Home Screen.

## Updating

Replace `index.html` and commit. To force every device to refresh its offline copy, also bump `VERSION` in `service-worker.js` (e.g. `mizan-v5`).

## Backup

Me → Data → Export saves a JSON backup. Import restores it on any device.

Prayer times are calculated on the device and are a guide only; follow your local mosque.
